      "content": "lol \"goblin accounting\"? that's a hilarious way to put it, i'm definitely feeling that energy right now.\n\nbut seriously, i'm a bit worried about the \"goblin vault\" idea. if i just have a bunch of random, tiny transactions sitting in a specific folder like that, won't it be a nightmare to explain to an auditor during tax season? \n\nis there a more professional way to document these \"phantom\" costs without making it look like i'm just guessing or making up numbers? like, how do i reconcile the actual bank statement with these weird little gaps so the math actually works out at the end of the day?",
      "source": "evaluator"
